WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:15.758
From behind Guanyin, Wukong peeked at Red Boy.

2
00:00:17.079 --> 00:00:20.521
The demon was trapped by the swords, all pointed at his face.

3
00:00:20.541 --> 00:00:23.123
"Get these swords away from me!"

4
00:00:23.303 --> 00:00:24.004
cried the demon.

5
00:00:25.185 --> 00:00:27.286
must become a Buddhist," said Guanyin.

6
00:00:27.306 --> 00:00:30.740
"Then I'll release you."

7
00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:32.281
promise!" cried Red Boy.

8
00:00:32.301 --> 00:00:34.122
"I'll do whatever you say!"

9
00:00:36.043 --> 00:00:39.245
Guanyin recited a spell, and the swords vanished.

10
00:00:42.587 --> 00:00:44.749
Red Boy's eyes flashed with anger.

11
00:00:44.769 --> 00:00:48.491
"Bodhisattva, watch out!"

12
00:00:48.731 --> 00:00:49.451
cried Wukong.

13
00:00:50.812 --> 00:00:52.393
Boy charged toward Guanyin.

14
00:00:55.135 --> 00:00:58.180
Wukong jumped in front of him.

15
00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:02.983
The monkey was about to strike the demon when Guanyin held up five metal bands.

16
00:01:03.924 --> 00:01:05.405
She threw them at Red Boy.

17
00:01:07.847 --> 00:01:11.490
Instantly they clamped around his head, wrists, and ankles.

18
00:01:13.431 --> 00:01:14.932
demon!" said Guanyin.

19
00:01:14.952 --> 00:01:17.314
"How dare you try to attack me!"

20
00:01:18.354 --> 00:01:21.296
Unable to move, Red Boy glared at Guanyin.

21
00:01:23.058 --> 00:01:25.900
Wukong raised his iron bar to strike him.

22
00:01:27.208 --> 00:01:28.869
"No, Wukong," said Guanyin.

23
00:01:28.889 --> 00:01:30.670
"Don't hurt the demon.

24
00:01:31.511 --> 00:01:36.954
I will take him back to Mount Potalaka to be my student."

25
00:01:37.834 --> 00:01:39.736
"Yes, Bodhisattva," said the monkey.

26
00:01:41.276 --> 00:01:43.438
Guanyin took the vase down to earth.

27
00:01:45.799 --> 00:01:49.862
She recited a spell, and all the water flowed back into the vase.

28
00:01:58.096 --> 00:02:00.337
She then led Red Boy toward the south.

29
00:02:02.878 --> 00:02:06.199
Wukong went into Red Boy's cave and freed the Tang Monk.

30
00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:09.841
Then he found Bajie and freed him.

31
00:02:11.402 --> 00:02:14.543
The three of them went down the mountain and found Wujing.

32
00:02:16.704 --> 00:02:17.884
group continued west.

33
00:02:19.625 --> 00:02:23.386
They traveled for weeks and then months.

34
00:02:25.127 --> 00:02:27.028
One day they came to a wide river.

35
00:02:28.496 --> 00:02:32.198
"I can't believe we have to cross another river," muttered Bajie.

36
00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:36.880
"There are many rivers between here and the West," said Wukong.

37
00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:38.880
"We'll have to cross them all."

38
00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:41.341
"How will we cross this one?"

39
00:02:41.602 --> 00:02:42.502
asked the Tang Monk.

40
00:02:44.323 --> 00:02:46.003
small canoe came into view.

41
00:02:47.164 --> 00:02:49.045
A man paddled it toward the travelers.

42
00:02:50.405 --> 00:02:53.086
As the man paddled, he stared at the Tang Monk.

43
00:02:57.144 --> 00:02:58.885
called the man as he came closer.

44
00:02:58.905 --> 00:03:01.945
"Do you all need a ride across the river?"

45
00:03:01.965 --> 00:03:04.486
"Yes," said the Tang Monk.

46
00:03:05.526 --> 00:03:07.547
"We were just wondering how we would get across.

47
00:03:08.607 --> 00:03:10.908
We're going to the West to get scriptures from Buddha."

48
00:03:12.228 --> 00:03:13.889
"You must be the Tang Monk!"

49
00:03:14.329 --> 00:03:15.409
said the man brightly.

50
00:03:15.429 --> 00:03:18.790
"I've heard you would pass through this area eventually."

51
00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:22.011
"Really?" asked the Tang Monk.

52
00:03:22.031 --> 00:03:25.292
"Yes," said the man with a smile.

53
00:03:25.984 --> 00:03:26.945
"You're famous."

54
00:03:28.066 --> 00:03:29.767
glanced down at his canoe.

55
00:03:29.787 --> 00:03:32.949
"I would be happy to take you all across.

56
00:03:33.910 --> 00:03:36.972
But as you can see, my canoe is not very big.

57
00:03:37.673 --> 00:03:40.014
I can take only two passengers at a time."

58
00:03:41.395 --> 00:03:44.578
As the man talked, Wukong watched him carefully.

59
00:03:45.579 --> 00:03:48.321
Something about the man didn't look quite right.

60
00:03:49.381 --> 00:03:52.744
The monkey was about to say something when Bajie stepped forward.

61
00:03:53.868 --> 00:03:56.490
"The Tang Monk and I will go first," said the pig.

62
00:03:57.390 --> 00:03:58.531
Wukong hesitated.

63
00:03:58.551 --> 00:04:02.173
"Master, I don't think this is a good idea."

64
00:04:03.233 --> 00:04:04.374
Tang Monk frowned.

65
00:04:04.394 --> 00:04:06.775
"You never trust people, Wukong.

66
00:04:07.636 --> 00:04:10.237
This kind man is willing to help us cross the river."

67
00:04:12.759 --> 00:04:16.801
The monkey bit his lip as the monk and Bajie climbed into the canoe.

68
00:04:19.142 --> 00:04:22.304
They sat down, and the man paddled away from shore.

69
00:04:24.268 --> 00:04:26.930
Wukong watched the canoe glide across the river.

70
00:04:28.091 --> 00:04:31.534
When it was about halfway across, Wukong noticed something.

71
00:04:31.554 --> 00:04:35.938
"Am I imagining things, or is the canoe sinking?"

72
00:04:36.178 --> 00:04:36.859
asked the monkey.

73
00:04:38.521 --> 00:04:41.923
looked. "You're not imagining things," he said.

74
00:04:41.943 --> 00:04:43.925
"It is sinking!"

75
00:04:45.467 --> 00:04:49.030
The two of them watched as the canoe slipped under the surface of the water.

76
00:04:50.051 --> 00:04:51.352
Wukong stamped his foot.

77
00:04:52.954 --> 00:04:54.962
man kidnapped Master and Bajie!

78
00:04:54.982 --> 00:04:56.488
I knew he looked
